<!doctype html>
<html lang="zh-CN">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>SXSEditor</title>
    <style>
      html, body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        overflow: hidden;
        /* Matches the BrowserWindow backgroundColor and the SVG solid fill
           (THEME.bgApp = #14141f = --bg-app in dark-aurora.theme.json), so
           the empty window -> painted-SVG transition is invisible. */
        background: #14141f;
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", "PingFang SC",
          "Microsoft YaHei", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
        color: #f4f4f8;
      }
      #splash-root {
        width: 100vw;
        height: 100vh;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <!--
      Inline SVG: renders on HTML parse, BEFORE any JS bundle loads or
      IPC round-trip completes. This is the key to "double-click →
      instant popup" — the user sees the branded splash the moment
      did-finish-load fires for the splash itself, with zero JS
      execution on the critical path.

      The version / build-date text is written DIRECTLY into the markup by
      scripts/generate-build-info.js at build time (and by prestart in dev).
      It used to be filled in by splash.js over IPC after first paint; that
      round-trip is now gone, which is what lets this window drop its
      preload entirely (see the note in webpack.renderer.config.js about
      splash_preload) and with it ~100ms of renderer-process startup on the
      critical path.

      ICON_SOURCE below is substituted at build time. webpack's HtmlWebpack-
      style substitution is not available for the webpack plugin's HTML
      pipeline, so generate-build-info.js writes the resolved relative path
      in as a literal (see the SPLASH_ICON comment there). The default
      "./SXS.png" is correct for both dev and packaged builds; the
      substitution exists only so a future non-standard asset layout does not
      need to touch this file.
    -->
    <div id="splash-root">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
           width="440" height="280" viewBox="0 0 440 280"
           role="img" aria-label="SXSEditor splash screen">

        <!-- Solid app background (matches --bg-app). -->
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="440" height="280" fill="#14141f" />

        <!-- 3px accent bar at the top, matching --toolbar-accent-line. -->
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="440" height="3" fill="#5b8def" />

        <!-- App icon (top-left, 64x64). Loaded by the SVG directly via a
             relative URL so it resolves in parallel with HTML parse. -->
        <image id="splash-icon" x="20" y="20" width="64" height="64"
               preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" href="__SPLASH_ICON__" />

        <!-- App name -->
        <text x="100" y="50"
              font-size="22" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="0.5"
              fill="#e0e0f0"
              font-family="-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', 'PingFang SC', 'Microsoft YaHei', sans-serif">
          SXSEditor
        </text>

        <!-- Tagline / brief introduction -->
        <text x="100" y="72"
              font-size="12" font-weight="400"
              fill="#8888a8"
              font-family="-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', 'PingFang SC', 'Microsoft YaHei', sans-serif">
          AI Singing Voice Synthesis Workstation
        </text>

        <!-- Footer divider -->
        <line x1="20" y1="240" x2="420" y2="240"
              stroke="#2a2a3d" stroke-width="1" />

        <!-- Version (left) — build-time substituted, no IPC needed. -->
        <text id="splash-version" x="20" y="262"
              font-size="11" font-weight="500"
              fill="#8888a8"
              font-family="-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', 'PingFang SC', 'Microsoft YaHei', sans-serif">__SPLASH_VERSION__</text>

        <!-- Build date (right) — build-time substituted, no IPC needed. -->
        <text id="splash-build-date" x="420" y="262" text-anchor="end"
              font-size="11" font-weight="400"
              fill="#8888a8"
              font-family="-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', 'PingFang SC', 'Microsoft YaHei', sans-serif">__SPLASH_BUILD_DATE__</text>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <!--
      No <script> tag on purpose.

      This window previously loaded splashPreload.js (to expose splashAPI)
      plus splash.js (to fill version/date/icon over IPC). Both are gone:
      the payload above is fully resolved at build time, so first paint needs
      no JavaScript at all. Removing the preload also removes the preload
      script compilation + execution from before-first-paint, measured at
      roughly 100ms of renderer startup on the critical path.

      If a future splash needs interactivity, reintroduce the preload and
      measure again — do not add script tags that block first paint.
    -->
  </body>
</html>